# Round XXV Track D §D-3: do-stmt-match variant of the compound-tail
# borrow-bind. `auto r = do:` newline `match n: case 1: &a else: &b` —
# D10(a) `E_LocalBorrowBind` fires at the outer decl (authoritative). ⚠
# The match arms must be INDENTED MULTI-LINE bodies — an inline `case X:
# <body>` in a do-tail stmt-match is a parse error regardless of `&`. Pre-
# fix the safety-pass mirror-walker also emitted `E_AmpInOperandPosition`
# on each arm-body `&a`/`&b`; post-fix the flag gates the mirror-walker
# emit, so the fixture asserts single-diagnostic (E_LocalBorrowBind
# present, E_AmpInOperandPosition ABSENT).

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] b = [4, 5]
    int n = 1
    auto r = do:
        match n:
            case 1:
                &a
            else:
                &b
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
